+// engine-patches/0413 (DM_PSO_USER_FIRST): this device's pso_user.tsv holds every row the game itself asked for, the seed's too, once each and in that order, it is written crash-safe,
+// and the prewarm walks it before the seed list. What it shows, on this Mac (the second half on its GPU, with synthetic shader libraries as t_pso_head's):
+//  - pso_user_record: a row the seed list holds is written (on) or skipped (DM_PSO_USER_FIRST=0, the old list), a row is written once, rows keep their order;
+//  - a file whose last row a killed process cut gets a line end first, and the cut row and the next stay two lines; a child process killed with SIGKILL while it writes rows leaves only
+//    whole rows; eight threads writing at once leave every row whole and once;
+//  - warm_paths: [this device's list, the seed] (on), [the seed, this device's list] (=0), [the seed] without a list;
+//  - warm_parse of [list, seed]: the list's tasks first in its order, then the seed's others in theirs, nothing twice;
+//  - the real prepare step with DM_PSO_PREPARE_PERCENT=25 (10 of 40 tasks): the head is the 10 tasks the list names (on), the seed's first 10 (=0); the tail then builds the rest, each once.
+#include "../nvn/nvn_mtl.m"
+#include <fcntl.h>
+#include <signal.h>
+#include <spawn.h>
